 :audit/conclusion
 {:all-keys-pqc-encrypted-at-rest? false
  :all-keys-rotation-configured? false
  :summary "kagi uses hybrid post-quantum cryptography for recipient DEK transport and ledger signatures, but not for every key or every storage boundary. kotoba retains quantum-vulnerable Ed25519/X25519 authority surfaces. kagitaba intentionally performs no cryptography. Only per-item DEK rotation exists, and it is manual."}
