 :findings
 [{:id :KKEY-001 :severity :critical
   :finding "The JVM method named argon2id does not implement Argon2id and ignores the requested memory and parallelism as security work factors."
   :impact "Offline guessing resistance is far below the documented 256 MiB Argon2id claim."
   :remediation "Use a reviewed Argon2id implementation, version KDF metadata, benchmark to roughly 0.5-1.0 seconds on the target device, and migrate envelopes after successful unlock. Fail closed if the real provider is unavailable."}
  {:id :KKEY-002 :severity :high
   :finding "Identity signing and KEM private material can be persisted as unencrypted base64 in identity.edn unless the optional SecretStore path is configured."
   :remediation "Make non-exportable OS keystore/HSM custody the default and refuse plaintext identity creation outside an explicit development mode. Inventory and migrate every existing identity."}
  {:id :KKEY-003 :severity :high
   :finding "There is no complete key registry containing key id, algorithm suite, epoch, creation time, activation time, originator expiry, retirement, revocation, custody, and parent key."
   :remediation "Add a versioned key registry and enforce state transitions at every encrypt, sign, decapsulate, unwrap, and verify boundary."}
  {:id :KKEY-004 :severity :high
   :finding "Item rotation is manual and share revocation only marks a grant revoked; it does not rotate the DEK or invalidate previously distributed envelopes/ciphertext."
   :remediation "On revoke, create a new item epoch and DEK, encrypt a new ciphertext version, and issue envelopes only to the remaining recipients. Treat old epochs as decrypt-only and reject them for current reads."}
  {:id :KKEY-005 :severity :high
   :finding "Ed25519 remains the DID/IPNS authority and CACAO signature, so the authority and authorization plane is not fully post-quantum."
   :remediation "Introduce a versioned hybrid authority document and dual-sign transitions; retain Ed25519 for compatibility only while requiring ML-DSA for new high-value decisions."}
  {:id :KKEY-006 :severity :medium
   :finding "The linear ledger hash chain is tamper-evident but has no key-epoch binding, fork rule, witness checkpoint, trusted timestamp, or old-to-new rotation certificate."
   :remediation "Adopt the rotation DAG specified by the companion ADR, periodically witness its Merkle root, and bind every fact signature to suite id, key id, epoch, and domain-separated canonical bytes."}
  {:id :KKEY-007 :severity :medium
   :finding "kagitaba accepts intentionally unencrypted 1PUX exports and returns plaintext data structures/bytes without lifecycle controls."
   :remediation "Require an explicit unsafe-import acknowledgement, stream directly to kagi sealing where possible, reject unsafe paths/oversized archives, avoid logs, and document secure source-file deletion as an operator step."}
  {:id :KKEY-008 :severity :medium
   :finding "Key bytes and plaintext are ordinary JVM byte arrays/Strings and are not reliably zeroized; CLI can print secrets to stdout and environment-based master secrets are supported."
   :remediation "Minimize lifetime and copies, avoid String conversion, isolate reveal in a short-lived process, prefer OS keychain/passkey/HSM handles, and reserve environment secrets for compatibility mode."}]
